EXT. HILLSIDE ABOVE THE LAKE - DUSK #11#

A small fire on the ground among the seated people. Lamps in hands. The lake is the colour of pewter.

ELEAZAR
After the swine, he goes home? No father in Israel would open his gate to him.

ELEAZAR
Write it down, Jotham. The elders will want every word.

JOTHAM
I have written nothing.

He looks at the old lines already cut in the wax, and smooths them flat with his thumb.

JOTHAM
Look at the publican.

Hezron weeps into his hands. Tirzah pulls one of his hands away from his face and holds it.

TIRZAH
Abba.

Jesus waits until Hezron's fingers close around his daughter's. Then he goes on, to Hezron now as much as to the gate.

JESUS
And he arose, and came to his father.

